\">χωρὶς ἡ τ. θεῶν</span> <b class=\"lex-tr\">the honour due</b> to them, <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">A.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">Ag.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">637</span> </span>, cf. <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">Ch.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">200</span> </span>; <span class=\"gk\">τιμὰς τὰς θεῶν πατεῖν</span> <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">S.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">Ant.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">745</span> </span>; <span class=\"gk\">τιμαὶ δαιμόνων</span> <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">E.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">Hipp.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">107</span> </span>: <span class=\"gk\">τιμῇ</span> <b class=\"lex-tr\">with honour, honourably</b>, <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">S.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">OC</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">381</span> </span> codd.; <span class=\"gk\">τιμῆς ἕνεκα</span> as <b class=\"lex-tr\">a mark of honour</b>, <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">X.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">An.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">7.3.28</span> </span>; <span class=\"gk\">τιμῇ προέξους'</span> <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">S.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">Ant.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">208</span> </span>. </div> <div class=\"lex-sense\" data-level=\"3\"><span class=\"lex-n\">2</span> <b class=\"lex-tr\">honour, dignity, lordship</b>, as the attribute of gods or kings, <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Il.</span> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">1.278</span> </span>, <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">9.498</span> </span>, etc.; <span class=\"gk\">θεῶν ἒξ ἔμμορε τιμῆς</span> <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Od.</span> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">5.335</span> </span>; <span class=\"gk\">τ. βασιληΐς</span> <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Il.</span> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">6.193</span> </span>, cf. <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Hes.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">Th.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">393</span> </span>, <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Pi.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">P.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">4.108</span> </span>, <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">A.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">Eu.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">228</span> </span> (pl.); <span class=\"gk\">Περσονόμος τ. μεγάλη</span> <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Id.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">Pers.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">919</span> </span> (anap.); <span class=\"gk\">δίθρονος.. καὶ δίσκηπτρος τ</span>. <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Id.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">Ag.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">44</span> </span> (anap.): generally, like γέρας, <b class=\"lex-tr\">prerogative</b> or <b class=\"lex-tr\">special attribute</b> of a king, and in pl. his <b class=\"lex-tr\">prerogatives</b>, <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Od.</span> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">1.117</span> </span>, <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Hes.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">Th.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">203</span> </span>, <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Thgn.</span> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">374</span> </span>, <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">S.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">OT</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">909</span> </span> (lyr.), etc.; <span class=\"gk\">βασιλικαὶ τ</span>. imperial <b class=\"lex-tr\">prerogatives</b>, <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\