x-cite-scope\">19</span> </span> (anap.), cf. <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Isoc.</span> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">9.81</span> </span>; <span class=\"gk\">ἐκβαλῶ σε ἐκ τῆς τιμῆς</span> <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">X.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">Cyr.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">1.3.9</span> </span>; <span class=\"gk\">τιμὰς ἴσχειν</span> hold the <b class=\"lex-tr\">office</b> of <span class=\"gk\">τιμοῦχος</span> (q.v.), <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">Jahresh.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">12.136</span> </span> (Erythrae, <span class=\"lex-cite-date\">v/iv B.C.</span>): generally, <b class=\"lex-tr\">office, task</b>, <span class=\"gk\">ἄχαρις τιμή</span> <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Hdt.</span> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">7.36</span> </span>:—also, </div> <div class=\"lex-sense\" data-level=\"4\"><span class=\"lex-n\">b</span> <b class=\"lex-tr\">a person in authority, an authority</b>, <span class=\"gk\">κλῦτε δὲ Γᾶ</span> (Ahrens for <span class=\"gk\">τὰ</span>) <span class=\"gk\"> χθονίων τε τιμαί</span> <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">A.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">Ch.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">399</span> </span> (lyr.); <span class=\"gk\">καὶ τὰ καρτερώτατα τιμαῖς ὑπείκει</span> yield to <b class=\"lex-tr\">authorities</b>, <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">S.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">Aj.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">670</span> </span>. </div> <div class=\"lex-sense\" data-level=\"3\"><span class=\"lex-n\">4</span> <b class=\"lex-tr\">present of honour, compliment, offering</b>, e.g. to the gods, <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Hes.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">Op.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">142</span> </span>, <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">A.</span